Key Responsibilities
1. MQ Environment Assessment & Analysis
•	Assess current-state MQ environments, including:
o	Queue Managers
o	Channels & Queues
o	Security configurations
o	System dependencies
•	Identify migration scope across applications, platforms, versions, and environments (DEV / UAT / PROD)
•	Analyze compatibility impacts, deprecated features, and enhancements in the target MQ version/platform
________________________________________
2. Discovery & Dependency Mapping
•	Perform detailed application dependency mapping to understand:
o	Message flows
o	Interfacing systems
•	Document all MQ objects and configurations required for migration
•	Collaborate with application owners to capture:
o	Message volume patterns
o	SLA requirements
o	Peak load characteristics
________________________________________
3. Migration Strategy Design & Coordination
•	Work closely with MQ Architects to define migration approaches:
o	In-place upgrade
o	Parallel build
o	Blue-Green deployment
o	Cloud migration
•	Ensure alignment with:
o	Enterprise architecture standards
o	Security policies
o	DR/HA requirements
•	Support design documentation for new MQ infrastructure:
o	Distributed systems
o	Containerized environments
o	Cloud MQ setups
________________________________________
4. Risk, Impact & Change Management
•	Conduct impact analysis for:
o	Message formats
o	Connectivity changes
o	SSL/TLS certificates
o	Access policies & routing paths
•	Identify risks and dependencies; track mitigation plans
•	Prepare and manage change control documentation
________________________________________
5. Testing & Validation Support
•	Define test scenarios and acceptance criteria for MQ migration
•	Coordinate end-to-end testing with application teams to validate:
o	Connectivity
o	Message delivery
o	Throughput & performance
o	System resilience
•	Monitor MQ logs, error queues, and alerts during testing cycles
________________________________________
6. Migration Execution Support
•	Assist engineering teams with:
o	Cutover planning
o	Rollback/fallback strategies
o	Migration execution coordination
•	Validate post-migration configurations:
o	Queues
o	Channels
o	Listeners
o	SSL/TLS setups
•	Support defect triage and root-cause analysis
________________________________________
7. Stakeholder Communication & Management
•	Facilitate:
o	Migration workshops
o	Readiness meetings
o	Status checkpoint calls
•	Communicate migration timelines, risks, and progress to stakeholders
•	Ensure application teams are fully prepared for migration activities
________________________________________
8. Documentation & Governance
•	Maintain detailed documentation:
o	Migration runbooks
o	Interface inventories
o	Routing diagrams
•	Ensure compliance with enterprise governance and audit standards
•	Update CMDB, knowledge bases, and operational documents post-migration
________________________________________
Essential Skills
•	Strong experience in IBM MQ architecture and administration
•	Expertise in MQ migration strategies and planning
•	Knowledge of:
o	Queue managers, channels, clustering
o	SSL/TLS and MQ security
o	Message persistence and routing
•	Experience with distributed, containerized, or cloud MQ environments
•	Strong analytical, troubleshooting, and stakeholder communication skills

